Figure Captions
Fig. 1. Overall framework and clinical deployment strategy of the study. A. Study
workflow: (a) Preparation of postoperative fluid attenuated inversion recovery (FLAIR)
images: Postoperative FLAIR images from four centers were divided into train,
validation, and independent test sets. Following preprocessing, peri-cavitary
hyperintense regions on FLAIR images were delineated. (b) Development of
DeepGBM-Recure: The system comprises an automated segmentation model based on
nnU-Net to delineate peri-cavitary hyperintense regions, a patient-level model using
Random Forest classifiers with the entire lesion as the analytical unit for individualized
recurrence risk stratification, and a voxel-level model employing supervoxels as the
analytical unit for spatial localization of high-risk recurrence subregions. (c) Validation
of DeepGBM-Recure: Model performance and clinical utility were evaluated using
receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curves, calibration curves, and decision curve
analysis, with heatmaps visualizing high-risk recurrence zones. B. Clinical Deployment
and Inference: Illustration of the real-time clinical implementation pipeline,
demonstrating seamless integration from magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) input to
risk-stratified therapeutic guidance.
Fig. 2. Predictive performance of patient-level model and voxel-level model. ROC
curves of random forest classifier in three study sets at patient-level (A) and voxel-level
model(B). Calibration curve (C) and decision curve (D) of patient-level model in test
set.
Fig. 3. Visualization of voxel-level model of representative cases in test set. For each
patient (left column: patient ID), three imaging panels are displayed from left to right:
postoperative FLAIR images prior to tumor recurrence, predicted recurrence
probability map (Red regions indicate high-risk areas for recurrence) and contrast
enhanced T1-weighted imaging (CE-T1WI) at tumor recurrence. Four patients on the
left side presented with early recurrence, with progression free survival (PFS) of 5-6
months, while other four patients on the right side exhibited non-early recurrence, with
PFS of 8-12 months.
Fig. 4. Two cases predicted by DeepGBM-Recure system and the hypothetical clinical
deployment. IDH, isocitrate dehydrogenase; MGMT, O6‐methylguanine‐DNA
methyltransferase; PFS, progression free survival; OS, overall survival.


